<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[FB          : Pneumatic Air Pressure Group Festo Cat3 e NoCat3
Last Change : 19.01.2017
Author      : Luca Borra / Ing.M.Padovani
v1.0        : Initial creation Oct, 10 2016.
v1.1        : New Release Jan, 19 2017 including: 
              1- iRqMovement
              2- DelayedPneuEmergency
              3- MSG Wait Pressure ON
v1.2        : New Release Jun, 20 2017 including: 
              1- i_TimePresetDOWNPressOK (ms) for Downstream Pressure OK
              2- q_xAirPressure_OFF
              

**************************************************************************
 This FB manages a Festo MS6-SV D-10V24 (Cat3) or a Standard NoCat3 Group
**************************************************************************

i_xEnableTypeCat3: this input defines if the Pneumatic Group is or not CAT3 
Type. If it is CAT3 the input must be TRUE.

i_xEnableAlrm_P_In: this input enables or disable the Alarm related to the
Air Pressure state at the INFEED of the Air Group. If the Pressure Switch of P 
IN exists, it can be enabled.

i_xAirPress_UPSTREAM: if the previous input is enabled, this input must be
connected with the signal of the UPSTREAM AIR PRESSURE SWITCH.

i_xAirPress_DOWNSTREAM: this input must ALWAYS be connected to the
DOWNSTREAM AIR PRESSURE SWITCH. It is always of present in any type of group.

i_TimePresetDOWNPressOK: this time (ms) represent the delay time before
to activate the output info #q_xDOWNSTREAM_AirCirc_ON.

i_xAirValvesPosSensors: this input exists only in the CAT3 air groups. The 
input connected represents the series of the two reed sensors which check the
real state of the two valves.

i_xMachineEnable: this input refers to the conditions which give the operator
the possibility to reset the alarm conditions and to activate the air flow.
Normally this info is: M1.2 in the standard groups, M1001.2 in the
Pallet Magazines groups.

i_xAirPressOperateCondit: this input changes depending on the machine type
and is subject to different conditions.
E.G.: General Air Group: M1.3 is the standard condition, sometimes it can
be needed a delayed conditions, such as the Delayed Safety Switch.
Pallet Magazine Air Group: in this case, being the Pallet Magazine Area
accessible trhough the Safety Light Barriers, the OSSD state of the Barriers
must be added in the input conditions. 

iq_xRqMovement: this input refers to the Request of any type of movement
done by the operator via the Touch Panel. Normally is associeted to M7.0.

iq_xRqPneumEmerg: this is the request of pneumatic emergency, whic can be
set inside the FB or coming from outside (it is an I/O memory). This memory
normally is set when a pneumatic movement is assumed to be faulty, thus
the Request of Pneumatic Emergency deactivate the air pressure flow.
For General Air Group M1.6 is the standard.
For Pallet Magazine Air Group M1001.6 is the standard.
Other cases to be evaulated time by time.

iq_xMSGWaitPneuPressON: MSG2. It means the air valve is activated but the
air pressure still haven't reached the expected level.

iq_xImmediateStopForAlrm: in case of dangerous conditions, the machine
must be stopped quickly. This memory is ment for the quick stop purpose.
For General Air Group M0.2 is the standard.
For Pallet Magazine Air Group M1000.2 is the standard.

iq_xPhaseStopForAlrm:  if a stop is needed, but there is no necessity of
immediate stop (such as not the dangerous conditions) the group can be
stopped with a procedure which allows the Stop in Phase procedure.
A standard case of use of this memory is an alarm occurring in one part
of the machine, which do not affect the main cycle function.
E.G.: the Pallet Magazine is off because of new pallet loading, and by
the same time the machine still works palletising the cases.
 
q_xDOWNSTREAM_AirCirc_ON: this output is not related to the type CAT3 o NOCAT3.
It represents the DOWNSTREAM air circuit at right air pressure level.

q_xActivateValve: this is the output to activate the solenoid valve NOCAT3
or the valves (2 valves) in CAT3.

q_xAlrmUPSTREAM_Pressure: this alarm depends from the presence of the
UPSTREAM pressure switch. If the pressure switch is present and the alarm is
enabled, the output alarm message works.
For General Air Group CAT3 type ALRM10 is the standard.

q_xAlrmPneuGroupDamage: This alarm is always present.
For General Air Group ALRM61 is the standard.
For Pallet Magazine Air Group ALRM261 is the standard.

q_xEPNCircuit_ON: this info gives a feedback regarding
the air circuit state.
For General Air Group M2.0 is the standard.
For Pallet Magazine Air Group M1002.0 is the standard.

q_xAirPressure_OFF: this info gives a feedback regarding the air pressure state.
It grants, checking also the CAT3 Reed Sensors that the air circuit is
really OFF, to avoid possible risks.
For General Air Group .... is the standard.
For Pallet Magazine Air Group ...... is the standard.

q_xAlrmDiagValvesCAT3: this alarm is active only if the input _xEnableTypeCat3
is TRUE and represent a cross check between the valve real position and its
expected position. If there is a misalignment between real and expected
position, this alarm comes out.
For General Air Group CAT3 type ALRM32 is the standard.
For Pallet Magazine Air Group CAT3 type ALRM260 is the standard.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(i_xAirPress_UPSTREAM)XIC(i_xEnableAlrm_P_IN)[MOVE(500,Ton_Alrm_UPSTREAM_Press.PRE) ,TON(Ton_Alrm_UPSTREAM_Press,?,?) ,XIC(Ton_Alrm_UPSTREAM_Press.DN) [OTE(q_xAlrm_UPSTREAMPressure) ,OTL(iq_xRqPneumEmerg) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(i_xMachineEnable) ,XIC(q_xActivateValve) ]XIC(i_xAirPressOperateCondit)XIO(L_PneumaticEmergency)OTE(q_xActivateValve);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(q_xActivateValve) XIO(i_xAirPress_DOWNSTREAM) OTL(L_MEM_AirCircuitOFF) ,XIC(q_xActivateValve) OTU(L_MEM_AirCircuitOFF) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(q_xActivateValve) XIC(q_xDOWNSTREAM_AirCirc_ON) OTL(L_MEM_AirCircuitON) ,XIO(q_xActivateValve) OTU(L_MEM_AirCircuitON) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(q_xActivateValve) XIC(i_xAirPress_DOWNSTREAM) ,XIC(q_xActivateValve) XIC(i_xAirPress_DOWNSTREAM) LE(Ton_DOWNSTREAM_AirCircON.PRE,0) ][MOVE(i_TimePresetDOWNPressOK,Ton_DOWNSTREAM_AirCircON.PRE) ,TON(Ton_DOWNSTREAM_AirCircON,?,?) ,XIC(Ton_DOWNSTREAM_AirCircON.DN) OTE(q_xDOWNSTREAM_AirCirc_ON) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(q_xActivateValve)XIO(q_xDOWNSTREAM_AirCirc_ON)XIC(i_xRqMovement)OTL(iq_xMSGWaitPneumPressON);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(q_xActivateValve) XIO(i_xAirPress_DOWNSTREAM) ,XIO(q_xActivateValve) XIC(i_xAirPress_DOWNSTREAM) ][MOVE(5000,Ton_Alrm_AirPressState.PRE) ,TON(Ton_Alrm_AirPressState,?,?) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(q_xActivateValve) XIC(i_xAirValvesPosSensors) ,XIO(q_xActivateValve) XIO(i_xAirValvesPosSensors) ]XIC(i_xEnableTypeCAT3)[MOVE(800,Ton_Alrm_ValveDiagnostic.PRE) ,TON(Ton_Alrm_ValveDiagnostic,?,?) ,XIC(Ton_Alrm_ValveDiagnostic.DN) [OTE(q_xAlrmDiagValvesCAT3) ,OTL(iq_xRqPneumEmerg) ,OTL(iq_xImmediateStopForAlrm) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(L_MEM_AirCircuitOFF) XIC(i_xAirPress_DOWNSTREAM) ,XIC(L_MEM_AirCircuitON) XIO(i_xAirPress_DOWNSTREAM) ,XIC(Ton_Alrm_AirPressState.DN) ][OTE(q_xAlrm_PneuGroupDamgage) ,OTL(iq_xRqPneumEmerg) ,OTL(iq_xImmediateStopForAlrm) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(iq_xRqPneumEmerg) ,XIC(L_MEM_AirCircuitOFF) XIC(L_MEM_AirCircuitON) ] OTL(L_AuxPneumaticEmergency) ,XIO(iq_xRqPneumEmerg) XIO(q_xDOWNSTREAM_AirCirc_ON) OTU(L_AuxPneumaticEmergency) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(L_AuxPneumaticEmergency)[MOVE(500,Ton_DelayPneuEmergency.PRE) ,TON(Ton_DelayPneuEmergency,?,?) ,XIC(Ton_DelayPneuEmergency.DN) OTE(L_PneumaticEmergency) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(L_PneumaticEmergency)OTU(iq_xRqPneumEmerg);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(L_PneumaticEmergency)[OTL(iq_xImmediateStopForAlrm) ,OTL(iq_xPhaseStopForAlrm) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(L_PneumaticEmergency)XIC(q_xDOWNSTREAM_AirCirc_ON)OTE(q_xEPN_Circuit_ON);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(q_xActivateValve)XIO(i_xAirPress_DOWNSTREAM)[XIC(i_xAirValvesPosSensors) ,XIO(i_xEnableTypeCAT3) ]OTE(q_xAirPressure_OFF);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Name="PowerFlex525" Class="Standard" Revision="1.1" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="false" CreatedDate="2008-01-15T10:31:04.156Z" CreatedBy="Not Available" EditedDate="2023-06-29T11:03:38.198Z" EditedBy="DESKTOP-I4HL37F\admin" SoftwareRevision="v32.01"
>
<Description>
<![CDATA[Pflex525 Ethernet Management
]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[V1.1 : 29/06/2023
Author: Utili 
Comment: Spostato ingresso pilz su Input per gestione separata


V1.0 : 03/09/2021
Author: Tiberia 
Comment: Aggiunto riferimento di velocità a 50Hz in                  modo da calcolarsi il fattore di conversione.
                 Velocità massima e minima verranno settati                 nei parametri dell'inverter come anche i valori                 di acc e dec. 
                Non più con un controllo esterno
]]>
</RevisionNote>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="EnableIn" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Input - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="EnableOut" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Output - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="I_Enable" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="true" Visible="true" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<DefaultData Format="L5K">
