<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(sDCS_CRS.S9100.DCS.O1)OSF(sDCS_CRS.axFTrig[1],sDCS_CRS.xFEdgeOperatorSide_PBSafetyRESET);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[*********************************************************************************************************************************************
ISO 13849-1 stipulates that instruction reset functions must occur on falling edge signals.
To comply with this requirement, add a One Shot Falling instruction to the rung immediately preceding the OutputEnable rung, 
then use the OSF instruction Output Bit tag as the Reset bit for the following rung. 
The CROut_Enable bit is then used to Enable the CROUT instruction.
*********************************************************************************************************************************************]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(sDCS_CRS.xFEdgeOperatorSide_PBSafetyRESET)XIO(sDCS_CRS.S9100.DCS.FP)OSF(sDCS_CRS.axFTrig[2],sDCS_CRS.FEdgeBlockReset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
